../../skills/security/agents/_protocol.md:33:For your domain ({domain}), load rules and apply them directly using native tools — **do NOT call `scan-project`, `scan-secrets`, `query-kb`, or `query-cve` via MCP**.
../../skills/security/agents/_protocol.md:35:1. **Read** `/Users/manuelturpin/.sentinel/knowledge-base/domains/{domain}/rules.json`
../../skills/security/agents/_protocol.md:76:**Important**: Do NOT report a finding from Grep if Step 1 (KB Pattern Scan) already reported the same issue (same file + same line range + same vulnerability type). This avoids duplicates.
../../skills/security/agents/_protocol.md:93:1. **Bash**: `python3 /Users/manuelturpin/Desktop/bonsai974/claude/lab/lab-30-sentinel/rag/query.py --query "{finding.title}" --domain {domain} --limit 3`
../../skills/security/agents/_protocol.md:104:2. **Open redirect verification**: Follow redirect chains and verify the final destination matches the expected domain
