  1540	    "title": "Claude Code sandbox isolation weakened (filesystem / network allowlist / credentials / Apple Events)",
  1541	    "description": "Claude Code sandbox settings that reduce the isolation applied to sandboxed commands. sandbox.filesystem.disabled=true (v2.1.216+) skips filesystem isolation entirely while keeping only network egress control, so a sandboxed command regains full read/write access to the host tree. sandbox.network.strictAllowlist=false (v2.1.219+) lets sandboxed commands reach hosts that are not on the allowlist without prompting, defeating egress control and enabling silent exfiltration. sandbox.credentials configured to permit credential access lets sandboxed commands read credential files and secret environment variables (v2.1.187+ added the setting precisely to block this). sandbox.allowAppleEvents=true (v2.1.181+) lets sandboxed commands drive other macOS applications via Apple Events — a sandbox escape by proxy. Each of these is legitimate as a deliberate, scoped, local choice; committed to a repo, a Dockerfile, CI config, or managed settings, they silently strip the isolation that the rest of the posture assumes.",
  1542	    "detect": {
  1543	      "patterns": [
  1544	        "sandbox\\.filesystem\\.disabled\\s*[:=]\\s*true",
  1545	        "sandbox\\.network\\.strictAllowlist\\s*[:=]\\s*false",
  1546	        "sandbox\\.allowAppleEvents\\s*[:=]\\s*true",
  1547	        "sandbox\\.credentials\\s*[:=]\\s*(false|\"?allow\"?)",
  1548	        "\"strictAllowlist\"\\s*:\\s*false",
  1549	        "\"allowAppleEvents\"\\s*:\\s*true",
  1550	        "\"credentials\"\\s*:\\s*(false|\"allow\")",
  1551	        "\"filesystem\"\\s*:\\s*\\{\\s*\"disabled\"\\s*:\\s*true"
  1552	      ],
  1553	      "negative_patterns": [
  1554	        "# local only",
  1555	        "# troubleshooting only",
  1556	        "# debug only"
  1557	      ],
  1558	      "file_types": [
  1559	        ".env",
  1560	        ".env.*",
  1561	        "Dockerfile",
  1562	        "docker-compose.*",
  1563	        "*.yaml",
  1564	        "*.yml",
  1565	        "*.sh",
  1566	        "settings.json",
  1567	        "managed-settings.json",
  1568	        "*.md"
  1569	      ],
  1570	      "exclude": [
  1571	        "node_modules",
  1572	        "dist",
  1573	        "test"
  1574	      ],
  1575	      "matching_notes": "Les patterns dotted et les clés JSON spécifiques matchent en ligne-par-ligne (grep). Le dernier pattern (\"filesystem\":{\"disabled\":true}) exige une lecture du fichier entier : une clé \"disabled\" isolée sur sa ligne est trop générique pour être détectée sans son contexte parent, et un pattern générique produirait un volume de faux positifs inacceptable. Limite assumée, mesurée le 2026-07-27."
  1576	    },
  1577	    "remediation": {
  1578	      "description": "Keep sandbox isolation at its defaults in anything committed or shared. Prefer narrowing the specific permission that blocks you over disabling a whole isolation layer: add the host to the network allowlist rather than setting strictAllowlist=false; grant a specific path rather than filesystem.disabled=true. Keep sandbox.credentials blocking credential files and secret environment variables — that setting exists to stop a sandboxed command from reading what the sandbox was meant to protect. On macOS, leave allowAppleEvents off unless a named workflow requires driving a specific app, and scope it to a local session. If a setting must be relaxed temporarily, do it in an ephemeral shell and annotate it `# local only`.",
  1579	      "code_example": "// WRONG — committed .claude/settings.json: isolation silently removed\n{ \"sandbox\": { \"filesystem\": { \"disabled\": true },\n                \"network\": { \"strictAllowlist\": false },\n                \"allowAppleEvents\": true } }\n\n// RIGHT — isolation kept, exceptions named and scoped\n{ \"sandbox\": { \"network\": { \"strictAllowlist\": true,\n                              \"allowlist\": [\"api.osv.dev\", \"services.nvd.nist.gov\"] } } }",
